#: 092a1e98a4f4466396bc6b5b7fd82a61
msgid ""
"You can set :file:`qvm-open-in-dvm.desktop` as the handler for a given MIME "
"type (such as :mimetype:`application/pdf`). This will cause all files of "
"that type to open in a disposable. This works in disposable templates too, "
"but be careful: if your disposable template is set to use :file:`qvm-open-in-"
"dvm.desktop` to open a certain kind of file, every disposable based on it "
"will be as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/disposable-customization.rst:117
#: f9ff4a0369e542b2bb5e91dcddf4d034
msgid ""
"If the disposable template is its own default disposable template (as is "
"often the case), this will result in a loop: :program:`qvm-open-in-dvm` will "
"attempt to execute :program:`qubes.OpenURL` in a new disposable, but that "
"will in turn execute :program:`qvm-open-in-dvm`. A question dialog will "
"appear to confirm if this is the intended behavior or not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/disposable-customization.rst:119
#: 2858fed83ad349f7819bccada61475d4
msgid ""
